SESR-M5 INT8 (sesr_m5_int8.onnx)

This file is the published NCHW INT8 ONNX graph from
https://huggingface.co/amd/ryzenai-sesr (sesr_nchw_int8.onnx),
Apache License 2.0. See LICENSE-SESR-Apache-2.0.txt.

The graph is fixed:
  input  Model::input_0  float32 NCHW 1x3x512x512  (about 0..255)
  output 254             float32 NCHW 1x3x1024x1024 (2x)

The model card also mentions 256x256 training tiles. This packaged
graph does not accept a 256 input. PixelRestore resamples one ROI
to 512x512, runs the 2x network, and blends the result back.
It estimates detail. It does not recover the original pixels.

Inference is on-device with ONNX Runtime (CPU execution provider).
The app does not download weights at runtime.

SESR was introduced in "Collapsible Linear Blocks for Super-Efficient
Super Resolution" (Bhardwaj et al., arXiv:2103.09404). The AMD Ryzen AI
export is a quantized ONNX build of that family. Do not assume an AMD
NPU is present on Android.
